# A prompt submitted while a turn is running. fx steers: during a tool-free
# answer it interrupts and continues with the new prompt at once; during a
# tool it shows the prompt above the composer as `┋ <prompt>` and delivers
# it after the tool. xfx keeps its queue -- the prompt runs as the next turn
# -- and shows it the same way, `┋ <prompt>`, until that turn starts and its
# card is written.
fx: gateway interrupt-steer-fx.json
xfx: gateway interrupt-steer-xfx.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
# The full-access warning is up from the first frame for 4 s (capfile.py
# TIMERS): the turn starts once it has come and gone, so no snap below
# races it.
until shown Full access
wait 2
until gone Full access
type stream please
key Enter
held
wait 1
type what are you doing
key Enter
# The steer stops the held stream and its own request is answered at once
# on both binaries: `steer-stream` is that answer, settled, taken by the
# screen rather than 0.4 s after Enter, which a loaded run sometimes
# reached before xfx had it (FLAKE-HINT4's sweeps, both directions).
until shown steered answer.
until gone Generating (
snap steer-stream
release
wait 12
snap steer-stream-done
type run it
key Enter
wait 1.5
type change tone
key Enter
wait 0.4
snap steer-tool
wait 6
snap steer-done
snapfull end
gwlog
